# Web Interface

The mail client provides a browser-based interface at `/mail`. You must be logged into your ship to access it.

## Pages

```
/mail              Inbox
/mail/sent         Sent messages
/mail/compose      Write a new message
/mail/read?id=X    Read message by ID
/mail/settings     Gateway, aliases, forwarding configuration
/mail/buy-alias    Purchase a short alias with ETH
/mail/gateway      Gateway admin (if enabled)
/mail/backup       Backup and restore mail data
/mail/help         Getting started guide
/mail/donate       Support the project
```

## Inbox

Messages sorted by date (newest first). Unread shown with `*` indicator. Sortable by date column. Sidebar with label filters.

Features:
- Click row to open message
- Click address to search by sender
- Delete button (x) on each row with confirmation
- Search by subject/from/body
- Pagination (25 per page)
- Batch select: mark read/unread, delete multiple
- Auto-refresh every 30 seconds (ETag-based, efficient)

## Reading a message

Shows sender, recipient, CC, date, labels, and message body. Markdown rendered (headings, bold, lists, blockquotes, links). Images hidden by default (Show/Hide toggle). View source for raw text.

Actions: Reply, Reply All, Forward, Mark Read/Unread, Delete, Back.

## Composing

Fields: To, CC/BCC (expandable), Subject, Body. Gateway selector if multiple domains configured. Auto-save drafts to localStorage.

## Labels

Organize mail with labels. Add from message view. Filter by label in sidebar. Labels colored automatically by name hash.

Dot-notation: use `shipname.label@domain` to auto-tag incoming mail. Multiple labels: `shipname.shop.receipts@domain`.

## Dark/Light theme

Toggle with sun/moon icon in navbar. Saved to localStorage. Auto-detects system preference.

## PWA

Install as standalone app: Chrome menu > Install. iPhone: Safari > Share > Add to Home Screen. Push notifications work from PWA.
